course: dictionary
lesson: 6309
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show you which one is meant. Mortal is a good example. It can mean something that will die one day, or something very great, like mortal danger. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «Shuffled off this mortal coil» is an old, joking way of saying someone has died. The words around mortal tell you the meaning, because the phrase is about dying. Then test it: put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Theo's big brother Callum has Mortal Kombat, a fighting game» uses mortal as part of a name. A name is not a meaning, so here you just learn what the game is. When mortal is a describing word, look for clues about death, danger, or how strong a feeling is.
fact: Mortal has several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant.
fact: Mortal means certain to die one day. Its opposite is immortal, which means never dying.
fact: In stories about gods, a mortal is a human being.
fact: Mortal can also mean very great or extreme, as in «mortal danger» or «mortal fear».
fact: «Shuffled off this mortal coil» means died; it comes from Shakespeare's Hamlet and is used jokingly.
exercise: In old stories, gods are immortal. What does mortal mean when it describes humans? | Gods who never die | *Human beings who will die one day | Very old stones | Animals that live in the sea
exercise: «She was in mortal danger when the bridge began to crack.» What does mortal mean here? | Causing death in a fight | Certain to die one day, like everyone | Very cold and wet | *Very great, extreme
exercise: «Shuffled off this mortal coil» is an old phrase used jokingly. What does it mean? | *Died | Went to bed early | Moved house | Danced happily
test: Which word means not living forever? | Ancient | *Mortal | Glum | Immortal
test: In old stories, gods live forever. What is a human called there? | Immortal | Ancient | *A mortal | A god
exam: Which meaning fits «a mortal enemy»? Put the meaning into the sentence and check. | Enemies who wear masks | *Enemies who hate each other forever | Friends who are very quiet | Enemies who live under the sea
